Rudy.

48
00:03:50,040 --> 00:03:54,560
Embarrassing you was the last thing I wanted to do. I'm so sorry.

49
00:03:55,180 --> 00:04:00,020
Rudy, stop. I'm not embarrassed about anything, okay? Go back to normal.

50
00:04:00,020 --> 00:04:03,540
As much as I would love to return to normal, I don't think I can.

51
00:04:03,700 --> 00:04:06,160
That's not what I mean. Just stop being so formal.

52
00:04:06,420 --> 00:04:09,280
Oh, right. I'm sorry. I'm getting kind of flustered.

53
00:04:09,760 --> 00:04:11,760
No more fancy talk from now on, okay?

54
00:04:11,880 --> 00:04:12,580
As you wish.

55
00:04:12,820 --> 00:04:13,920
You're still doing it.

56
00:04:14,220 --> 00:04:16,100
That one's not so bad, is it?

57
00:04:18,080 --> 00:04:23,980
Thank you for this pendant, by the way.

58
00:04:24,880 --> 00:04:28,880
I'm glad it got to you. I always assumed it was long gone.

59
00:04:28,880 --> 00:04:31,300
Lilia held onto it for us.

60
00:04:31,660 --> 00:04:32,400
That's sweet.

61
00:04:33,120 --> 00:04:36,260
So anyway, why do you disguise yourself as a boy?

62
00:04:36,720 --> 00:04:40,040
Right, all of that. I don't even know where to start.

63
00:04:40,040 --> 00:04:49,620
Well, I watched you being taken away in the carriage that day. You were unconscious. I was so shocked that I attacked Paul.

64
00:04:49,880 --> 00:04:51,020
Really? You?

65
00:04:51,020 --> 00:05:01,180
I mean, it was really sudden. And I was confused and angry. But that day, I promised myself that I'd get strong enough to save you.

66
00:05:01,180 --> 00:05:04,100
My mind was made up.

67
00:05:04,100 --> 00:05:10,660
I started studying. I practiced magic. I even asked Lilia to teach me some etiquette.

68
00:05:10,660 --> 00:05:17,320
I just wanted to catch up to you. I wanted to be worthy. I worked so hard.

69
00:05:17,320 --> 00:05:29,800
Then came the mass teleportation. It warped me to the royal palace, where I met Princess Ariel and Luke.

70
00:05:30,340 --> 00:05:33,520
What happened between then and university is kind of a long story.

71
00:05:34,060 --> 00:05:37,800
But I was so glad when I saw your name on a list of potential new students.

72
00:05:38,500 --> 00:05:39,880
Thank you for being alive.

73
00:05:40,560 --> 00:05:41,060
You're welcome.

74
00:05:41,540 --> 00:05:42,380
And thank you, too.

75
00:05:42,380 --> 00:05:47,620
And I get why, but it was so weird to hear you introduce yourself to me like a stranger.

76
00:05:48,060 --> 00:05:51,860
I bet. I'm sorry. I just can't believe you didn't say something sooner.

77
00:05:52,300 --> 00:05:56,160
I guess I should have. I just couldn't work up the courage. Sorry.

78
00:05:57,080 --> 00:06:00,740
That's okay. If I weren't so oblivious, you wouldn't have had to.

79
00:06:04,940 --> 00:06:08,160
Ah! Rudy, you can't do that in public.

80
00:06:08,580 --> 00:06:09,740
Yeah, I'm sorry.

81
00:06:09,740 --> 00:06:13,480
So I do get some response. I just can't control it.

82
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:15,420
But progress is progress.

83
00:06:16,040 --> 00:06:18,080
And now I can safely say I'm on the mend.

84
00:06:19,460 --> 00:06:20,580
All thanks to her.

85
00:06:21,520 --> 00:06:22,900
What are you staring at?

86
00:06:22,900 --> 00:06:38,200
Well, I've got business with the Princess, so I should go.

87
00:06:38,660 --> 00:06:39,000
Okay.

88
00:06:39,920 --> 00:06:41,160
And I guess...

89
00:06:41,160 --> 00:06:42,840
We'll see each other soon?

90
00:06:43,200 --> 00:06:44,120
Oh, right.

91
00:06:44,460 --> 00:06:44,780
Yes.

92
00:06:45,240 --> 00:06:46,040
Uh, guess so.

93
00:06:46,420 --> 00:06:48,340
Or I would like that very much anyway.

94
00:06:48,340 --> 00:06:59,760
I wish I had some kind of medicine for Rudy's condition.

95
00:06:59,760 --> 00:07:11,180
So you failed, I take it?

96
00:07:11,580 --> 00:07:13,180
Well, no. I wouldn't say that.

97
00:07:13,360 --> 00:07:14,920
And was a bad plan in hindsight.

98
00:07:15,560 --> 00:07:17,400
Even if there was a risk of freezing,

99
00:07:17,660 --> 00:07:19,600
I suppose it's expecting a lot of someone

100
00:07:19,600 --> 00:07:21,600
to tear the clothing off a friend like that.

101
00:07:22,880 --> 00:07:25,860
Sylphie, just tell us exactly what happened, please.

102
00:07:25,860 --> 00:07:27,820
Um, okay.

103
00:07:31,820 --> 00:07:33,500
You can't be serious.

104
00:07:33,760 --> 00:07:34,040
Huh?

105
00:07:34,360 --> 00:07:36,260
No, that's why he's at the university.

106
00:07:36,520 --> 00:07:39,060
He's looking for a way to cure his impotence.

107
00:07:40,280 --> 00:07:41,300
Just imagine.

108
00:07:41,760 --> 00:07:44,560
To be so useless in the one moment it really counts.

109
00:07:45,200 --> 00:07:48,060
Goodness, I may have rather overestimated this rudious fellow.

110
00:07:48,060 --> 00:07:51,180
I don't think you're being fair.

111
00:07:51,360 --> 00:07:51,480
Huh?

112
00:07:52,260 --> 00:07:54,760
There are times when a man can't help it.

113
00:07:55,280 --> 00:07:57,000
It's not as though Rudy has spurned her

114
00:07:57,000 --> 00:07:58,900
or failed to make love to her by choice.

115
00:08:00,480 --> 00:08:04,160
In fact, this could explain why he's been so hesitant.

116
00:08:04,620 --> 00:08:05,760
He's afraid to disappoint.

117
00:08:06,880 --> 00:08:07,400
Sure.

118
00:08:07,400 --> 00:08:10,900
I've always wondered why he looked so insecure.

119
00:08:11,300 --> 00:08:12,440
So meek and withdrawn.

120
00:08:12,960 --> 00:08:13,740
That poor fellow.

121
00:08:14,280 --> 00:08:16,340
He must have come here out of sheer desperation

122
00:08:16,340 --> 00:08:18,180
with nowhere else to turn for help.

123
00:08:22,040 --> 00:08:23,620
I beg your pardon then.

124
00:08:23,860 --> 00:08:25,800
It would appear I spoke too strongly.

125
00:08:26,320 --> 00:08:26,980
That's all right.

126
00:08:27,440 --> 00:08:29,900
It's only natural that your highness wouldn't understand.

127
00:08:30,740 --> 00:08:33,320
Sylphie, how do you feel about all this

128
00:08:33,320 --> 00:08:35,140
and would you want to help cure him?

129
00:08:35,140 --> 00:08:37,520
Uh, uh, mm-hmm.

130
00:08:38,420 --> 00:08:41,060
He's been taking the entire situation to heart.

131
00:08:41,520 --> 00:08:44,560
So yeah, of course I want to do what I can for him.

132
00:08:45,080 --> 00:08:46,720
But are you committed to knowing

133
00:08:46,720 --> 00:08:48,240
that it may prove to be a challenge?

134
00:08:48,960 --> 00:08:49,440
Yes.

135
00:08:49,960 --> 00:08:51,040
I'll do anything.

136
00:08:52,600 --> 00:08:53,560
All right then.

137
00:08:54,080 --> 00:08:55,620
I may have something for you.

138
00:08:56,060 --> 00:08:57,120
I'll have to go get it.

139
00:08:57,880 --> 00:08:59,620
Your highness, excuse me.

140
00:08:59,620 --> 00:09:05,300
Again, I do hope you can forgive me.

141
00:09:05,620 --> 00:09:07,160
I misspoke about Rudeus.

142
00:09:07,460 --> 00:09:08,180
It's fine.

143
00:09:08,280 --> 00:09:09,020
I'm not upset.

144
00:09:09,380 --> 00:09:11,320
Well, Luke obviously has some kind of plan

145
00:09:11,320 --> 00:09:12,440
he'd like to set in motion.

146
00:09:12,860 --> 00:09:13,980
But as it happens,

147
00:09:14,080 --> 00:09:16,500
I actually know several cures for impotence myself.

148
00:09:16,960 --> 00:09:17,320
Really?

149
00:09:17,480 --> 00:09:18,140
What are they?

150
00:09:18,560 --> 00:09:18,840
Okay.

151
00:09:18,840 --> 00:09:21,840
What are you doing?

152
00:09:22,120 --> 00:09:23,980
I am returning to where I began

153
00:09:23,980 --> 00:09:25,880
and practicing incantationless magic.

154
00:09:26,600 --> 00:09:28,220
Then keep it down.

155
00:09:28,480 --> 00:09:30,160
Give me practice that part of it more.

156
00:09:30,540 --> 00:09:31,960
Go, Master Sanobo!

157
00:09:32,560 --> 00:09:33,760
Getting them drunk first,

158
00:09:33,920 --> 00:09:34,220
you should be like...

159
00:09:34,220 --> 00:09:34,540
I'm back.

160
00:09:34,620 --> 00:09:35,240
Thanks for waiting.

161
00:09:35,480 --> 00:09:35,660
...alcohol.

162
00:09:35,660 --> 00:09:36,380
Of course.

163
00:09:36,800 --> 00:09:38,900
But then you suddenly notice how hot it is.

164
00:09:39,100 --> 00:09:41,020
Bare your shoulders a little and voila.

165
00:09:41,400 --> 00:09:43,140
And you think that's enough to do it?

166
00:09:43,220 --> 00:09:44,820
Oh, there's no doubt in my mind.

167
00:09:45,180 --> 00:09:46,980
You have the perfect look to pull that off.

168
00:09:47,280 --> 00:09:48,520
All you need is opportunity.

169
00:09:49,180 --> 00:09:50,940
And perhaps a few choice words

170
00:09:50,940 --> 00:09:52,140
prepared to seal the deal.

171
00:09:52,680 --> 00:09:53,020
No.

172
00:09:53,320 --> 00:09:55,260
Complaining of heat in the dead of winter like that

173
00:09:55,260 --> 00:09:56,580
would get you taken to a medic.

174
00:09:57,780 --> 00:09:59,260
But in any season,

175
00:09:59,460 --> 00:10:01,400
Sophie doesn't have the figure for feminine wiles.

176
00:10:01,400 --> 00:10:05,720
You needn't put it so brutishly, Luke.

177
00:10:06,280 --> 00:10:07,640
Your Highness, the gray rat men

178
00:10:07,640 --> 00:10:09,820
have been drawn to buck some women for generations.

179
00:10:10,340 --> 00:10:11,940
If he's anything like the rest of us,

180
00:10:11,980 --> 00:10:12,600
it won't work.

181
00:10:13,040 --> 00:10:15,440
Personally, I feel no attraction to Sophie at all

182
00:10:15,440 --> 00:10:16,420
and I never have.

183
00:10:19,100 --> 00:10:20,100
However...

184
00:10:20,100 --> 00:10:24,040
Wow, what is that for?

185
00:10:24,480 --> 00:10:27,660
This lady's is a powerful Fitoan aphrodisiac.

186
00:10:28,220 --> 00:10:28,780
Behold.

187
00:10:29,340 --> 00:10:30,240
You're joking.

188
00:10:30,240 --> 00:10:32,220
It was at one time

189
00:10:32,220 --> 00:10:33,220
widely distributed,

190
00:10:33,820 --> 00:10:35,840
but the facility where it was manufactured

191
00:10:35,840 --> 00:10:37,080
and the recipe they used

192
00:10:37,080 --> 00:10:38,900
were lost to the mass teleportation,

193
00:10:39,040 --> 00:10:39,700
so eventually,

194
00:10:40,280 --> 00:10:41,360
the asking price soared

195
00:10:41,360 --> 00:10:43,560
to over 100 gold pieces per bottle.

196
00:10:44,660 --> 00:10:46,160
I've been holding on to this

197
00:10:46,160 --> 00:10:47,460
in case I ever found myself

198
00:10:47,460 --> 00:10:48,780
in urgent need of money.

199
00:10:49,700 --> 00:10:50,340
But...

200
00:10:50,340 --> 00:10:51,640
you should take it.

201
00:10:52,040 --> 00:10:53,540
It's so valuable, though.

202
00:10:53,980 --> 00:10:54,840
Are you sure?

203
00:10:55,260 --> 00:10:55,780
Of course.

204
00:10:56,660 --> 00:10:57,240
But listen,

205
00:10:57,660 --> 00:10:58,980
any man who drinks this stuff

206
00:10:58,980 --> 00:11:00,480
will completely lose control.

207
00:11:01,560 --> 00:11:03,100
So if you can't keep up,

208
00:11:03,300 --> 00:11:04,980
you may want to drink some of it yourself.

209
00:11:05,820 --> 00:11:07,780
And keep in mind that your first time

210
00:11:07,780 --> 00:11:09,240
won't go the way you've envisioned.

211
00:11:09,800 --> 00:11:10,600
It never does.

212
00:11:11,400 --> 00:11:12,380
Thank you, Luke.

213
00:11:12,380 --> 00:11:15,760
I appreciate it.

214
00:11:15,760 --> 00:11:17,340
Oh, think nothing of it.

215
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:19,740
You've saved my life often enough.

216
00:11:19,820 --> 00:11:20,920
I definitely owed you.

217
00:11:22,920 --> 00:11:25,280
I love how you two have become friends.

218
00:11:25,880 --> 00:11:27,660
Here, let me chip in, too.

219
00:11:29,500 --> 00:11:30,620
But, Princess,

220
00:11:31,040 --> 00:11:32,460
isn't this your personal money?

221
00:11:33,180 --> 00:11:35,220
Yes, my spending money for this month.

222
00:11:35,860 --> 00:11:36,680
Please take it.

223
00:11:36,980 --> 00:11:38,000
At this point in the game,

224
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:39,220
it's the only helpful thing

225
00:11:39,220 --> 00:11:40,300
I have left to give.

226
00:11:41,860 --> 00:11:42,660
Thank you.

227
00:11:43,180 --> 00:11:44,300
Thank you so much.

228
00:11:44,920 --> 00:11:46,660
Benevolent is always your grace.

229
00:11:47,500 --> 00:11:47,980
Sylvie.

230
00:11:48,900 --> 00:11:49,700
Best of luck.

231
00:11:50,720 --> 00:11:51,160
Okay.

232
00:11:52,160 --> 00:11:52,960
Here I go.

233
00:11:52,960 --> 00:12:02,580
Princess Ariel picked out

234
00:12:02,580 --> 00:12:03,860
some new underwear for me.

235
00:12:04,400 --> 00:12:06,100
And I have the aphrodisiac

236
00:12:06,100 --> 00:12:07,000
that Luke gave me.

237
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:08,360
Okay.

238
00:12:12,300 --> 00:12:13,280
Mom, Dad,

239
00:12:13,640 --> 00:12:14,740
give me your blessing.

240
00:12:15,440 --> 00:12:15,760
Tonight,

241
00:12:15,940 --> 00:12:17,360
I'm going to become a woman.

242
00:12:22,160 --> 00:12:22,640
Yes?

243
00:12:22,960 --> 00:12:23,980
Oh, hey,

244
00:12:24,120 --> 00:12:24,840
Syl...

245
00:12:24,840 --> 00:12:26,060
Master Fitz, rather.

246
00:12:26,660 --> 00:12:27,040
Please,

247
00:12:27,360 --> 00:12:28,120
come on in.

248
00:12:29,020 --> 00:12:29,460
Thanks.

249
00:12:37,140 --> 00:12:38,000
So, what's up?

250
00:12:38,400 --> 00:12:39,860
You were so tired earlier.

251
00:12:40,300 --> 00:12:41,920
I thought you'd be going straight to bed.

252
00:12:42,460 --> 00:12:42,820
Well,

253
00:12:43,120 --> 00:12:45,640
I came to stay the night.

254
00:12:45,880 --> 00:12:46,060
Huh?

255
00:12:47,320 --> 00:12:47,800
Oh.

256
00:12:48,580 --> 00:12:49,060
Okay.

257
00:12:49,640 --> 00:12:50,360
If you want,

258
00:12:50,600 --> 00:12:51,840
come in and sit down, then.

259
00:12:51,840 --> 00:13:04,080
What is that?

260
00:13:04,440 --> 00:13:04,780
Oh,

261
00:13:04,920 --> 00:13:06,400
I brought that for us to share.

262
00:13:06,860 --> 00:13:07,500
After all,

263
00:13:07,560 --> 00:13:08,400
we ought to do something

264
00:13:08,400 --> 00:13:09,560
to celebrate our reunion,

265
00:13:09,740 --> 00:13:09,960
right?

266
00:13:10,220 --> 00:13:10,500
Oh.

267
00:13:10,500 --> 00:13:11,680
Yeah, true.

268
00:13:11,680 --> 00:13:13,620
We should commemorate the occasion.

269
00:13:17,240 --> 00:13:17,800
Here.

270
00:13:18,460 --> 00:13:19,780
You need cups, right?

271
00:13:19,980 --> 00:13:20,720
I have plenty.

272
00:13:20,940 --> 00:13:22,000
I eat in here a lot.

273
00:13:23,000 --> 00:13:23,840
Well then,

274
00:13:24,280 --> 00:13:25,260
here's to old friends

275
00:13:25,260 --> 00:13:26,140
from Buena Village

276
00:13:26,140 --> 00:13:27,380
reunited at last.

277
00:13:27,640 --> 00:13:27,940
Cheers.

278
00:13:28,660 --> 00:13:29,640
And to our future,

279
00:13:29,780 --> 00:13:30,100
Sylphie.

280
00:13:30,880 --> 00:13:31,420
Yeah,

281
00:13:31,760 --> 00:13:32,200
cheers.

282
00:13:32,200 --> 00:13:34,660
Our future?

283
00:13:35,120 --> 00:13:37,780
Rudy says the most embarrassing stuff sometimes.

284
